    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d512">

                <pb facs="0473" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg357"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/115.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Dominican
                        Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 24, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 12th instant, wherein you discuss the
                    Dominican-Haitian boundary <pb facs="0474" n="358" xml:id="pg358"/> question and
                    inform the Department that certain Haitian authorities have committed acts in
                    contravention of the status quo which was agreed by both Governments should be
                    observed pending a definite settlement of the boundary dispute.</p>
                <p>In reply you are informed that the Department will give this matter its prompt
                    and careful consideration and will take such action as the facts may seem to
                    warrant.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
